# Build context exclusions. Two blocks below are the point -- the dumps and
# .env, each carrying live credential material. The rest is caches and
# host-local state.
#
# Bare names are written `**/`-prefixed. .gitignore matches a bare name at ANY
# depth, so anything gitignored is invisible in `git status` wherever it sits;
# a root-anchored rule here would admit the nested copy of a file no commit
# will ever show you. `.git` included: a vendored clone under packages/ shows
# in `git status` as one collapsed entry, and an unprefixed rule would put its
# whole object database -- history included -- in the context.
#
# Path rules like docs/screenshots stay anchored, because they name a place.
**/.git
**/.venv
**/.local
**/.worktrees
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/.pytest_cache
**/.mypy_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/.hypothesis
**/*.egg-info
**/.claude
**/logs
**/dist
**/.coverage
docs/screenshots

# Database dumps: 41 MB carrying users.password_hash and api_keys.key_hash.
# beacon.dump is a directory; the first rule matches it, the globs catch a
# dump dropped loose anywhere in the tree. Kept in sync with .gitignore, and neither
# file's rules can be complete -- nothing here produces dumps, so the names
# are typed by hand.
**/beacon.dump
**/*.dump
**/*.dump.*
**/*.backup
**/*.sql.gz

# .env is the dangerous one, and it is worse than a leak.
#
# It holds a live BEACON_JUDGE_API_KEY and REPO_GUARD_NAME_PATTERNS. `COPY . .`
# would bake both into the image pushed to ECR, and they would not sit there
# inert: api/config.py sets `env_file=".env"` and this image's WORKDIR is
# /app, so the DEPLOYED container would read it and drive the LLM judge
# against the workstation's endpoint on that key.
#
# `**/` and not a bare name: .gitignore's `.env` matches at ANY depth, so a
# file at packages/beacon_ui/.env is invisible to git. A root-anchored rule
# here would let exactly that file into the image -- gitignored, so no commit
# ever shows it, and unexcluded, so every build carries it.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
**/*.pem
**/*.key
